.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-SETTINGS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-settings
.Nd the Patina desktop's Settings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -page Ar page
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the desktop's Settings window, for what needs more than the desktop's
menu.
Its pages:
.Bl -tag -width "Night Light"
.It Appearance
The skin every piece of the shell wears, and its skins folder; and gaps
around tiled windows and the bar, with how big they are and how round the
floating bar's corners are, written to
.Ic [gaps]
in the compositor's config.
.It Bar
What the window tabs show (icons, titles, or both), which edge the bar sits
on, and its config file for everything else.
Its layout: one bar, or split into its parts (experimental), each placed by
dragging it on a map of the screen, where it snaps to the nearest spot, or
from a list.
.It Wallpaper
The default, and the images in
.Pa ~/Pictures/Wallpapers
and the system's backgrounds.
.It Keyboard
The keyboard layouts Ctrl+Space steps through, in order: each moved up or
down, removed, or switched to, and more added from those XKB offers, found
by name; and how soon and how fast a held key repeats.
While the compositor's config has no layouts it shows the system's, from
.Pa /etc/default/keyboard ,
and the first change copies them into
.Ic [keyboard] .
Changing the list goes back to the first layout.
.It Night Light
Off, always on, or on a schedule, and how warm.
It shows whether this screen can be warmed, whether it's on now, with a
button to turn it off until the schedule next changes, and which apps are
holding it off.
.It Power
When the screen turns off without input, from never to 15 minutes, and
whether that locks it; and the power modes this machine has, through
power-profiles-daemon, why performance is held back, and which apps hold
a mode.
.It Processes
What the compositor started: each one's state, PID, uptime and restarts,
with Restart and Stop.
A click on a name opens a window following its output.
Under
.Xr patina-session 1 ,
Restart Desktop restarts the compositor and everything with it, once
confirmed.
Settings can't restart itself.
.El
.Pp
Settings changes the files the settings live in, keeping the rest of each:
the bar's config for the skin and wallpaper, and
.Ic [night_light] ,
.Ic [gaps] ,
.Ic [screen]
and
.Ic [keyboard]
in the compositor's.
Those watching them change at once.
Night Light's state, the layout in use and the processes come from the
compositor over the session bus; nested in another desktop, the pages say what isn't there.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -page Ar page
Open at
.Ar page :
.Cm appearance
(the default),
.Cm bar ,
.Cm wallpaper ,
.Cm keyboard ,
.Cm night-light ,
.Cm power
or
.Cm processes .
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/config.toml
.Ic skin
and
.Ic wallpaper .
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-compositor/config.toml
.Ic [night_light] ,
.Ic [screen] off_after
and
.Ic [lock] on_screen_off .
.It Pa ~/.local/share/applications/com.sectorflabs.Settings.desktop
Its launcher entry, so the launcher and the bar know it by name and icon,
shown only on the Patina desktop;
.Ql make install
puts it there, with its icon in
.Pa ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/ .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-menu 1 ,
.Xr patina-night-light 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
